{{! A page documenting something the standard client does not ship says so with

        :page-marketplace: hop-misc-lint

    the id the marketplace installs by, so the note can give the exact command
    rather than send the reader off to look it up. Sits above the engine tags:
    whether you can install a thing at all comes before which engines it runs
    on. Absent on a page, this renders nothing. }}
{{#with page.attributes.marketplace}}
<aside class="marketplace" aria-labelledby="marketplace-note">
  <p class="marketplace__label" id="marketplace-note">
    <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path d="M1.6 4.2h8.8l-.7 5.2a1 1 0 0 1-1 .85H3.3a1 1 0 0 1-1-.85zM4.2 4.2a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 3.6 0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>
    Marketplace plugin
  </p>
  <p class="marketplace__body">
    This is not part of the standard Apache Hop client. Install it via the
    marketplace or use <code>hop marketplace install {{this}}</code>.
  </p>
</aside>
{{/with}}
